定时任务配置说明\n\n一、作用\n- cron 是定时任务子系统的全局开关与历:
Scheduled task configuration

Purpose
cron controls global scheduled-task activation and history retention. Tasks created with cron_add / cron_update depend on it. This section controls whether tasks run and how much history is retained, not task expressions.

Fields
1) enabled: boolean. true continuously scans and triggers due tasks; false prevents the Cron scheduler from starting, while keeping task definitions in the workspace.
2) max_run_history: integer, maximum history entries per task; default 50. Older records are removed first when the limit is exceeded.

Examples
A: Recommended default
{
  "cron": {
    "enabled": true,
    "max_run_history": 50
  }
}

B: Higher audit retention
{
  "cron": {
    "enabled": true,
    "max_run_history": 200
  }
}

C: Temporarily disable scheduling without deleting definitions
{
  "cron": {
    "enabled": false,
    "max_run_history": 50
  }
}

Recommendations
Development/test: use 20–50 history entries for faster iteration and less noise. Production: keep enabled=true to avoid missed tasks; use 50–200 entries according to audit needs. More history improves traceability but increases storage and query costs; 30–50 may suffice for recent failures.

Troubleshooting tasks that do not run on time
1) Confirm cron.enabled=true.
2) Check the task is enabled and its expression is valid.
3) Confirm the main process is running; scheduling may have stopped with it.
4) Inspect recent run history to distinguish missing triggers from execution failures.
5) Confirm Gateway availability and successful settings persistence, then restart and inspect logs.
